{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfqhZaB8pVpHhW1dCqTyT","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I approved LLR-312, but TC-254 is still not blessed. The amendment is `VERDICT: MEANING rows=1` and first approval is `OUTCOME: APPROVE rows=1`. Both commits carry the `WI: WI-866` trailer, and the pre-commit hooks passed.\n\n**Amendment: TC-254 changed meaning, and I didn't bless it.** The lane fixed both problems from the first sitting. TC-254 now cites the two refused-target tests and states the link case exactly. Everything new matches its cited tests except one phrase. The Expected cell now claims \"the mint **and** close preflight every affected specification before writing\", but every preflight the test case actually exercises is at the close.\n- The one test that shows the mint refusing as a whole is `test_a_row_claimed_between_close_and_merge_refuses_the_whole_mint`.\n- No test case cites it.\n\n**First approval: LLR-312 is approved.** Each of its three clauses now has its own TC-254 Method clause and cited test:\n- validate before the first write;\n- one planned sequence per spec, so every blocker on a waiter lands;\n- apply over the current file, so redirected links survive.\n\nTC-254's remaining problem is about the mint, which LLR-210 owns, not this row.\n\n**Commits:**\n- `48184a4e` — the verdict, plus a text-only follow-up in WI-866's spec `## Dispositions`. It asks the lane to drop \"mint and\" from Expected, or cite the mint test with a Method clause, then bring TC-254 back for re-attestation. The intake parser reads it cleanly.\n- `a3bc6a06` — the approval act. Only LLR-312's `Status` moved from `Drafted` to `Approved`. The snapshot was `--approves \"docs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml=WI-866\"`; it recorded act 64 with `approved = [\"LLR-312\"]` and copied only the LLR registry. I checked that the copy matches the live registry.\n\nTC-254 stays drifted from its anchor until it